course: dictionary
lesson: 3716
title: Flexible: bending, changing and willing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flexible means it can bend or change easily without breaking or getting stuck. The same word can describe a material, a body, a plan or a person. Use the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Japan has strict earthquake rules, and many buildings have flexible frames that let them move without breaking.» Here flexible means the frame can bend and move safely. Try the swap: bendy frames that move without breaking still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Stretching after sport helps keep you flexible.» Here flexible describes a body that can bend and stretch easily. Words like flexible hours or flexible thinking use the same idea: something that can change to suit new needs.
fact: Flexible means able to bend or change easily without breaking.
fact: Glass is rigid, or stiff, and rubber is flexible; that is a useful pair to remember.
fact: «Flexible hours» means hours that can change to suit people, though they are often irregular with no guaranteed pay.
fact: «Flexible thinking» means being willing to change your plans or ideas.
fact: Stretching helps keep you flexible, but studies show it does very little to stop next-day soreness.
exercise: «The tapir has a short flexible snout.» What does flexible mean here? | Hidden under water | Painted in bright colours | Very heavy and hard | *Able to bend and move easily
exercise: In science, rubber is compared with glass. Which one is flexible? | *Rubber | Glass | Concrete
exercise: «Flexible hours» means what? | Hours of bright sunshine | Hours that never change at all | Hours spent asleep | *Hours that can change to suit people's needs
test: Ms Patel says, «We have flexible plans for the trip, so we can change them if it rains.» What does flexible plans mean? | Plans that are only for sunny days | *Plans that can change to suit new situations | Plans that are fixed and cannot change | Plans written in ink
test: A flexible person is someone who is what? | Someone who cannot bend at all | *Willing to change their plans or ideas | Someone who never moves from one spot | Someone who shouts loudly at everyone
exam: Which word is the opposite of flexible, as in the glass and rubber comparison? | Stretchy | Loose | *Rigid, like glass | Bendy
